{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act pre-offer criminal record inquiry ban","requirement":"A housing provider must not require an applicant to complete a housing application that asks about criminal record before making a conditional offer. Limited inquiries about certain drug and sex-offender matters are allowed.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All rental dwelling units except owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units. Applies to housing providers including landlords, owners, lessors, sublessors, assignees, and agents.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."},"exemptions":"A dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; certain inquiries about methamphetamine manufacture in federally assisted housing and lifetime sex offender registration are permitted.","penalty":"Monetary penalties up to $1,000, $5,000, or $10,000 based on prior violations in five/seven years; director may order cease-and-desist, compliance reporting, or other remedies.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to complete any housing application that includes any inquiries regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to the provision of a conditional offer,","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act limits on considering criminal records","requirement":"A housing provider may not evaluate certain criminal records, including non-convictions, expunged, pardoned, vacated, juvenile, or sealed records. After a conditional offer, only specified convictions within lookback periods may be considered, with an individualized assessment.","key_value":"6 years for first-degree; 4 years for second/third-degree; 1 year for fourth-degree","coverage_conditions":"All rental dwelling units except owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units. Applies to housing providers including landlords, owners, lessors, sublessors, assignees, and agents.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."},"exemptions":"A dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; certain inquiries about methamphetamine manufacture in federally assisted housing and lifetime sex offender registration are permitted.","penalty":"Monetary penalties up to $1,000, $5,000, or $10,000 based on prior violations in five/seven years; director may order cease-and-desist, compliance reporting, or other remedies.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-56","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not, either before or after the issuance of a conditional offer, evaluate an applicant based on any of the following types of criminal records: (1) arrests or charges that have not resulted in a criminal conviction; (2) expunged convictions; (3) convictions erased through executive pardon; (4) vacated and otherwise legally nullified convictions; (5) juvenile adjudications of delinquency; and (6) records that have been sealed.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act advertisement restriction","requirement":"A housing provider must not publish or circulate housing advertisements stating that applicants with arrests or convictions will not be considered, except for specified drug-related and sex-offender registration matters.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All rental dwelling units except owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units. Applies to housing providers including landlords, owners, lessors, sublessors, assignees, and agents.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."},"exemptions":"A dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; certain inquiries about methamphetamine manufacture in federally assisted housing and lifetime sex offender registration are permitted.","penalty":"Monetary penalties up to $1,000, $5,000, or $10,000 based on prior violations in five/seven years; director may order cease-and-desist, compliance reporting, or other remedies.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-58","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not knowingly or purposefully publish, or cause to be published, any housing advertisement that explicitly provides that the housing provider will not consider any applicant who has been arrested or convicted of one or more crimes or offenses,","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act drug and alcohol test prohibition","requirement":"A housing provider must not require an applicant to submit to a drug or alcohol test or request consent to obtain information from a drug abuse treatment facility.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All rental dwelling units except owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units. Applies to housing providers including landlords, owners, lessors, sublessors, assignees, and agents.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."},"exemptions":"A dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; certain inquiries about methamphetamine manufacture in federally assisted housing and lifetime sex offender registration are permitted.","penalty":"Monetary penalties up to $1,000, $5,000, or $10,000 based on prior violations in five/seven years; director may order cease-and-desist, compliance reporting, or other remedies.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-60","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to submit to a drug or alcohol test, or request the applicant’s consent to obtain information from a drug abuse treatment facility.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether criminal history is part of its eligibility criteria and that the applicant may provide evidence of inaccuracies or rehabilitation/mitigating factors.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All rental dwelling units except owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units. Applies to housing providers including landlords, owners, lessors, sublessors, assignees, and agents.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."},"exemptions":"A dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; certain inquiries about methamphetamine manufacture in federally assisted housing and lifetime sex offender registration are permitted.","penalty":"Monetary penalties up to $1,000, $5,000, or $10,000 based on prior violations; director may require return of the application fee and other remedies.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant:","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction after successful appeal","requirement":"If a housing provider successfully appeals a director’s order and a court overturns it, the provider may evict a former applicant who resides in the unit because of that order, with at least 45 days’ notice, notwithstanding the Anti-Eviction Act.","key_value":"45 days’ notice","coverage_conditions":"All rental dwelling units except owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units. Applies to housing providers including landlords, owners, lessors, sublessors, assignees, and agents.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."},"exemptions":"A dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; certain inquiries about methamphetamine manufacture in federally assisted housing and lifetime sex offender registration are permitted.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-63","quoted_span":"a determination that the housing provider did not violate the provisions of this act as evidenced by such successful appeal shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction;","interaction":"Overrides the Anti-Eviction Act, P.L.1974, c.49 (C.2A:18-61.1 et seq.), for this eviction.","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
